# .gitattributes -- normalise line endings and mark binary files.
#
# Why this exists: Git stores line endings differently on Windows (CRLF) and
# Linux/macOS (LF). Without this file, a file can flip between the two depending
# on who last touched it. That matters here because the golden-master test
# compares committed CSV fixtures: a line-ending change would fail the
# comparison for a reason that has nothing to do with the numbers.
#
# Rule: text files are stored in the repository with LF, and checked out with
# the platform's native ending. The golden CSV fixtures are pinned to LF so the
# comparison is stable across machines.

# Default: let Git normalise text files to LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Golden-master fixtures: pin to LF so the byte comparison is machine-independent.
tests/fixtures/golden/** text eol=lf

# Windows launchers: keep CRLF so they run correctly in cmd.exe.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never touch these.
*.xlsx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
